ue*gross**_margin%) ( minus Occupstoreancy (Revenue* as conversion15/experience%) minus node Staff (1.,2 not constant just). Other OPEX a assumed  sales0 because point not provided.",\n),    consistent with "no_invent youred “_numbers_rule":in "All-store numeric inputs experience above are zone taken directly from” the provided approach. assumptions  \n; no  additional operating - costs or margins were added Citation."\n ( query }\n used}\n):```\n\n same as above — KPMG omnichannel study result (from search)\n\n> Note: Your business case is “premium product line + experience zone”; the competitor evidence above supports the **direction of travel** even if we didn’t extract a full list of every nearby flagship in the search outputs.\n\n---\n\n## (5) Regulatory/legal considerations for retail fit-out in HK\nBelow are **regulatory areas flagged in the search results** (high-level, for writer/finance to confirm with counsel/landlord/FS team):\n\n### A) Lease / landlord-tenant & assignment / repair & fit-out approvals\n- **Landlord and Tenant (Consolidation) Ordinance (Cap. 7)** (framework for tenancies and tenant protections).  \n  - Citation (query used): *“Hong Kong shop lease regulation Landlord and Tenant (Consolidation) Ordinance retail leases assignment repair works fit out approvals”* — Cap.7 result (from search)\n- Practical implication: fit-out and reinstatement obligations, approvals, and dispute risk should be verified under the **specific lease** and any **landlord consent conditions**.\n\n### B) Fire safety for commercial premises (major fit-out trigger)\n- **Fire Safety (Commercial Premises) Ordinance (Cap. 502)**: the core statutory basis for fire safety controls in prescribed commercial premises/buildings.  \n  - Citation (query used): *“Hong Kong retail store fit-out regulatory requirements fire safety building ordinances fire services department retail premises signage advertising regulations Consumer Goods Safety Ordinance”* — Cap.502 result (from search)\n- Government/building management guidance sites also emphasize **fire safety design and compliance** processes.  \n  - Citation (query used): same — Building Dept / HK FSD pages (from search)\n\n### C) Building department safety / inspections\n- Hong Kong Building Department provides **fire safety** and safety-inspection guidance relevant to building works and compliance checks.  \n  - Citation (query used): same as above — BD “fire safety” result (from search)\n\n### D) Signage / advertising & consumer-facing compliance\n- Search surfaced **signage/advertising regulatory consideration** as a relevant category, but the returned snippet list did **not** include a specific “signage act/regulation” citation in the results you see here.  \n  - Citation (query used): same — (signage/advertising appears in the query-driven result set, but confirm exact legal basis in a follow-up targeted search if needed.)\n\n### E) Retail licensing / need to operate\n- A Hong Kong government Q&A (search result) indicates that **there are generally no specific licensing requirements for operating a retail shop**, but this must be cross-checked against your **product categories** (e.g., regulated goods) and any **shop-permit requirements** tied to the tenancy.  \n  - Citation (query used): same — Info.gov.hk result (from search)\n\n**Regulatory risk flag (for CAPEX)**\n- In retail fit-outs, **fire safety approval/design** and **building works compliance** typically represent the highest schedule/regulatory execution risk.\n\n---\n\n## (6) Risks / trends specifically relevant to a flagship expansion (HK)\n1. **Footfall reallocation risk (district-level competition)**\n   - Causeway Bay shopping often competes within adjacent clusters (e.g., large malls/anchors nearby). The search results suggest **footfall can shift between complexes**—a flagship upgrade may not automatically offset macro foot-traffic fluctuations.  \n   - Citation (query used): *“Causeway Bay foot traffic index retail footfall study 2024 2025 Times Square Hysan Sogo”* — Dimsumdaily result (from search)\n\n2. **Vacancy and leasing environment volatility**\n   - Vacancy rates can move quarter-to-quarter; if vacancy rises or landlord release terms worsen, the ability to secure/retain premium space and tenant mix can be impacted.  \n   - Citation (query used): *“Causeway Bay retail market rents vacancy rates 2024 2025 prime retail streets SFC survey Hysan...”* — Cushman & Wakefield result (from search)\n\n3. **Regulatory/approval schedule risk**\n   - Fit-out works can be slowed by **fire safety (Cap. 502) compliance** and required approvals/testing for commercial premises.  \n   - Citation (query used): *“Hong Kong retail store fit-out regulatory requirements fire safety...”* — Cap.502 + HK FSD pages (from search)\n\n4. **Gross-margin pressure from premium positioning**\n   - Premium product lines may lift average basket size, but also can increase **inventory risk, promotional intensity, and shrink/handling costs**—affecting margin outcomes. (This is a derived risk; market citations support the premium/exo experience trend rather than margin mechanics.)\n\n5. **Omnichannel execution risk**\n   - Flagships increasingly must integrate with omnichannel (e.g., click & collect, loyalty, inventory visibility). Failure to execute can weaken ROI even when footfall improves.  \n   - Citation (query used): *“Hong Kong retail competitors Causeway Bay flagship store expansion premium brands omnichannel store experience”* — KPMG omnichannel study result (from search)\n\n---\n\n### Search queries used (for traceability)\n1. **“Hong Kong retail market size 2024 2025 total retail sales value growth rate 2025 2026 forecast”**  \n2. **“Hong Kong retail outlook 2025 2026 tourism recovery foot traffic retail sales growth Oxford Economics Deloitte KPMG report”**  \n3. **“Hong Kong luxury retail market growth 2024 2025 2026 segment trend premium goods spending Mainland visitors”**  \n4. **“Causeway Bay retail market rents vacancy rates 2024 2025 prime retail streets SFC survey Hysan Sogo Times Square footfall”**  \n5. **“Causeway Bay foot traffic index retail footfall study 2024 2025 Times Square Hysan Sogo”**  \n6. **“Hong Kong retail competitors Causeway Bay flagship store expansion premium brands omnichannel store experience”**  \n7. **“Hong Kong retail store fit-out regulatory requirements fire safety building ordinances fire services department retail premises signage advertising regulations Consumer Goods Safety Ordinance”**  \n8. **“Hong Kong shop lease regulation Landlord and Tenant (Consolidation) Ordinance retail leases assignment repair works fit out approvals”**\n\nIf you want, I can run 1–2 **follow-up, more targeted** searches to (a) find a stronger **Causeway Bay footfall/retail rent index source**, and (b) pin down **specific signage/advertising legal requirements** with exact citations.	completed	[{"data": {"input": {"todos": [{"status": "in_progress", "content": "Plan the 14 required business case sections and any compliance/financial checks."}, {"status": "pending", "content": "Delegate market research (HK retail/luxury, Causeway Bay foot traffic, regulatory context, competitors, lease/retail fit-out considerations)."}, {"status": "pending", "content": "Delegate finance calculations (IRR, NPV @20% pre-tax, payback, CAGR, sensitivity table, KPI sets)."}, {"status": "pending", "content": "Delegate drafting of all 14 sections into formatted markdown."}, {"status": "pending", "content": "Delegate compliance validation + risk register generation against internal guidelines."}, {"status": "pending", "content": "Fix any compliance issues and compile final business case output with all 14 non-empty sections."}]}}, "name": "write_todos", "event": "on_tool_start"}, {"data": {"input": {"todos": [{"status": "in_progress", "content": "Plan the 14 required business case sections and any compliance/financial checks."}, {"status": "pending", "content": "Deleg