demonstrates the overall quality of a building, either a new or refurbished.\\n   Source: https://www.beamsociety.org.hk/files/BEAM_Plus_For_New_Buildings_Version_1_2.pdf\\n\\n3. **The Ultimate Guide to BEAM Plus Certification in Hong Kong**\\n   2 avr. 2025 — BEAM Plus assigns ratings to buildings based on their overall performance across various sustainability criteria. These ratings provide a clear ...\\n   Source: https://www.cim.io/blog/the-ultimate-guide-to-beam-plus-certification-in-hong-kong\\n\\n4. **Green Certification | Hong Kong | Global Sustainable ...**\\n   BEAM Plus. Building Environmental Assessment Method (BEAM) Plus is the leading environmental assessment tool for buildings in Hong Kong.\\n   Source: https://resourcehub.bakermckenzie.com/en/resources/global-sustainable-buildings/asia-pacific/hong-kong/topics/green-certification\\n\\n5. **[Selected Buildings and Brands for Hong Kong Green ...**\\n   26 août 2025 — BEAM Plus develops scoring criteria tailored to Hong Kong's subtropical climate, urban density, and user habits. BEAM Plus certification covers ...\\n   Source: https://hkenergyaudit.com/en/blogs/news/green-cert-apply-and-consultation\\n\\n### Related topics: Building Environmental Assessment Method (BEAM Plus for Existing Buildings), BEAM Plus New building, BEAM plus nb 2.0 Manual, BEAM Plus Hong Kong, BEAM Plus Building list\\n", "artifact": null, "tool_call_id": "call_UaU51eU6n9571eWXxHvbGtAv", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}}}, "name": "market_research", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"query": "Hong Kong store formats experiential retail trends interactive in-store events omnichannel"}, "output": {"id": null, "name": "market_research", "type": "tool", "status": "success", "content": "## Market Research: Hong Kong store formats experiential retail trends interactive in-store events omnichannel\\n\\n### Top Search Results\\n\\n1. **Retail is evolving faster than ever and In-store Asia 2026 ...**\\n   The future of retail includes embracing ecosystems and the experience economy, reconfiguring stores, and preparing for #Web3 and the #metaverse.\\n   Source: https://www.facebook.com/euroshop.tradefair/posts/retail-is-evolving-faster-than-ever-and-in-store-asia-2026-makes-that-shift-very/1287151366880870/\\n\\n2. **KPMG China's Post**\\n   Data-driven experiential displays are transforming retail into something far more immersive than simple transactions. When digital meets ...\\n   Source: https://www.linkedin.com/posts/kpmg-china_retail-is-evolving-are-you-ready-for-the-activity-7389466073831624704-3SKY\\n\\n3. **Retail Marketing 2019 tackles Hong Kong's challenges to ...**\\n   4 abr 2019 — The highlight C-suite panel \\"Hong Kong - cross-channel strategies and how to hybridise a physical and online store experience\\", tackled the ...\\n   Source: https://www.marketing-interactive.com/retail-marketing-2019-tackles-hong-kongs-challenges-to-innovate\\n\\n4. **How to Use Experiential Retail**\\n   Discover how experiential retail blends entertainment and shopping to create immersive, personalized, and loyalty-boosting experiences.\\n   Source: https://mailchimp.com/resources/experiential-retail/\\n\\n5. **Hong Kong Experiential Retail Report 2023 | CN**\\n   21 nov 2023 — In this report, we examine the trends and statistics surrounding the evolving retail preferences of both tourists and locals, including the ...\\n   Source: https://www.cushmanwakefield.com/en/greater-china/insights/hong-kong-experiential-retail-report-2023\\n", "artifact": null, "tool_call_id": "call_cjfqVrulEfVQ7CzWiuXpc6zw", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}}}, "name": "market_research", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"query": "Hong Kong fire safety code requirements for shop premises sprinkler smoke detectors means of escape"}, "output": {"id": null, "name": "market_research", "type": "tool", "status": "success", "content": "## Market Research: Hong Kong fire safety code requirements for shop premises sprinkler smoke detectors means of escape\\n\\n### Top Search Results\\n\\n1. **CODES OF PRACTICE FOR MINIMUM FIRE SERVICE ...**\\n   This Code of Practice shall be titled “Minimum Fire Service Installations and Equipment” hereinafter referred to as “The Code”. 1.2 Definitions. “Building” ...\\n   Source: https://www.hkfsd.gov.hk/eng/source/safety/File2022.pdf\\n\\n2. **Code of Practice for Fire Safety in Buildings 2011 (2024 ...**\\n   Fire safety in buildings is determined by a number of factors: the provisions of means of escape in case of fire, the ability for a building to resist the ...\\n   Source: https://www.bd.gov.hk/doc/en/resources/codes-and-references/code-and-design-manuals/fs_code2011.pdf\\n\\n3. **FSD Hong Kong Office Fit-Outs: Fire Services ...**\\n   12 Mar 2026 — Means of escape requirements govern the layout of the tenanted space, including maximum travel distances to exits, the width of escape routes, ...\\n   Source: https://www.facilitatecorp.com/fire-services-department-requirements-for-hong-kong-office-fit-outs/\\n\\n4. **Cap. 572 Fire Safety (Buildings) Ordinance**\\n   13 Des 2024 — The purpose of this Ordinance is to provide better protection from the risk of fire for occupants and users of, and visitors to, certain kinds of composite ...\\n   Source: https://www.elegislation.gov.hk/hk/cap572\\n\\n5. **Review on the local Code of Practice for the Provision ...**\\n   11 Okt 2025 — The development of Engineering Performance-Based Fire Codes (EPBFC) is essential for Hong Kong's fire safety regulations. The Means of Escape ...\\n   Source: https://www.academia.edu/72206474/Review_on_the_local_Code_of_Practice_for_the_Provision_of_Means_of_Escape\\n\\n### Related topics: Exit sign REQUIREMENT Hong Kong, Code of Practice for Fire Safety in Buildings, Street Fire hydrant requirement, Fire Services standard requirements of emergency electrical generator, Hose reel cabinet size\\n", "artifact": null, "tool_call_id": "call_jM2xaGOlL3Vg1wePywhvPzwI", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}}}, "name": "market_research", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"query": "Causeway Bay competitor landscape premium retailers brands flagship stores experiential retail examples"}, "output": {"id": null, "name": "market_research", "type": "tool", "status": "success", "content": "## Market Research: Causeway Bay competitor landscape premium retailers brands flagship stores experiential retail examples\\n\\n### Top Search Results\\n\\n1. **9 Best Places to Go Shopping in Causeway Bay**\\n   Lee Gardens One to Six is a swanky shopping mall with 6 separate buildings, each of which carries ultra-luxe fashion, jewellery and homeware brands. Popular ...Read more\\n   Source: https://www.hoteles.com/go/hong-kong/best-causeway-bay-shopping\\n\\n2. **Causeway Bay Luxury Shopping Guide 2025: Hong Kong's ...**\\n   Discover Causeway Bay's premium shopping destinations featuring SOGO, Times Square, and luxury brand boutiques. Complete guide to high-end shopping in Hong ...\\n   Source: https://www.ladies-market.hk/causeway-bay-luxury-shopping-guide\\n\\n3. **Causeway Bay vs Hong Kong Shopping Districts Comparison ...**\\n   Aug 31, 2025 — The Landmark: Chanel, Hermès, Louis Vuitton flagship stores · IFC Mall: Apple Store, premium international brands · Prince's Building: Cartier, ...Read more\\n   Source: https://www.causeway-bay-hk.com/causeway-bay-vs-hong-kong-shopping-districts-comparison\\n\\n4. **Top 10 Retail Stores in Hong Kong**\\n   Apr 20, 2025 — 10 prominent retail stores and shopping destinations in Hong Kong that showcase the city's diverse and dynamic retail landscape:​\\n   Source: https://asiapro-distribution.com/top-10-retail-stores-in-hong-kong/\\n\\n5. **9 Best Places to Go Shopping in Causeway Bay**\\n   Lee Gardens One to Six is a swanky shopping mall with 6 separate buildings, each of which carries ultra-luxe fashion, jewelry and homeware brands. Popular ...Read more\\n   Source: https://www.hotels.com/go/hong-kong/best-causeway-bay-shopping\\n\\n### Related topics: Cheap shopping in Causeway Bay, Causeway Bay clothing stores, Causeway Bay shopping mall, Causeway Bay shopping Street, Causeway Bay Centre shopping Arcade\\n", "artifact": null, "tool_call_id": "call_1wZtD8mmGhbqJQ18P07OHI7m", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}}}, "name": "market_research", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"query": "Hong Kong labour law requirements for retail employees minimum wage working hours event staff"}, "output": {"id": null, "name": "market_research", "type": "tool", "status": "success", "content": "## Market Research: Hong Kong labour law requirements for retail employees minimum wage working hours event staff\\n\\n### Top Search Results\\n\\n1. **A Concise Guide to the Employment Ordinance**\\n   the employee has met one of the working hours requirements: (i) he has worked for at least 17 hours in each week; or. (ii) (where he has worked less than 17 ...\\n   Source: https://www.labour.gov.hk/eng/public/wcp/ConciseGuide/EO_guide_full.pdf\\n\\n2. **Hong Kong's Labor Laws**\\n   Hong Kong does not have any statutory limits to working hours for adults, nor does it have any regulations on overtime compensation. For minors, the Employment ...\\n   Source: https://www.china-briefing.com/doing-business-guide/hong-kong/human-resources-and-payroll/labor-law\\n\\n3. **Labour Legislation & Guidelines - Employment**\\n   Find answers to frequently asked questions about legislation on employment, employees' compensation and occupational safety and health. Statutory Minimum Wage.\\n   Source: https://www.gov.hk/en/residents/employment/labour/index.htm\\n\\n4. **Statutory Minimum Wage**\\n   The monthly monetary cap on the requirement for employers to record the total number of hours worked by employees is also raised to $17,600 per month in tandem ...\\n   Source: https://www.labour.gov.hk/eng/news/mwo.htm\\n\\n5. **Understanding and Complying with Hong Kong's Minimum ...**\\n   ١٥‏/٠٨‏/٢٠٢٤ — As of 1 May 2023, the statutory minimum wage (SMW) in Hong Kong is set at HKD 40 per hour. This rate applies uniformly across Hong Kong, with no variation by ...\\n   Source: https://www.woodburnglobal.com/post/understanding-and-complying-with-hong-kong-s-minimum-wage-laws\\n\\n### Related topics: Hong Kong labor law for domestic helper, Minimum Wage in Hong Kong per month, Minimum Wage Hong Kong 2026, Hong Kong Labour law termination, How much minimum wage in Hong Kong for domestic helper\\n", "artifact": null, "tool_call_id": "call_m5q9WXTjcOsHQQrhp9leTzC6", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}}}, "name": "market_research", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"query": "Hong Kong retail market size 2024 2025 value growth rate sources"}, "output": {"id": null, "name": "market_research", "type": "tool", "status": "success", "content": "## Market Research: Hong Kong retail market size 2024 2025 value growth rate sources\\n\\n### Top Search Results\\n\\n1. **Hong Kong: retail sales value growth 2025**\\n   In 2025, the total retail sales value in Hong Kong increased by around one percent compared to the previous year. The total retail sales value in Hong Kong ...\\n   Source: https://www.statista.com/statistics/620955/hong-kong-retail-sales-value-growth/?srsltid=AfmBOorizKVrwkahqCfFWGriV4u2hNmFDs2oI76kqQ_10RRshxFAqMHU\\n\\n2. **Provisional statistics of retail sales for November 2025**\\n   2 ene 2026 — The revised estimate of the value of total retail sales in October 2025 increased by 6.9% compared with a year earlier. For the first 11 months ...\\n   Source: https://www.censtatd.gov.hk/en/press_release_detail.html?id=5717\\n\\n3. **Hong Kong Retail Market (2025-2031) | Trends & Size**\\n   Historical Data and Forecast of Hong Kong Retail Market Revenues & Volume By Supermarkets/Hypermarkets for the Period 2021-2031; Historical Data and Forecast of ...\\n   Source: https://www.6wresearch.com/industry-report/hong-kong-retail-market\\n\\n4. **Hong Kong Retailing Market Research Reports & Analysis ...**\\n   In 2025, apparel and footwear in Hong Kong, China experienced a 2% decline in retail current value sales to reach HKD52,385 million. This downturn was ...\\n   Source: https://www.marketresearch.com/seek/Retailing-Hong-Kong/206/1223/1.html\\n\\n5. **Provisional statistics of retail sales for December 2025 and ...**\\n   The revised estimate of the value of total retail sales in November 2025 increased by 6.5% compared with a year earlier. Of the total retail ...\\n   Source: https://www.info.gov.hk/gia/general/202602/03/P2026020300456.htm\\n\\n### Related topics: Hong Kong retail sales 2025, Hong Kong retail sales 2024, Hong Kong retail Statistics, Hong Kong retail sales decline, Hong kong retail sales 2023\\n", "artifact": null, "tool_call_id": "call_GCg0TKlMBvrOckbGj5gIPK0D", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}}}, "name": "market_research", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"query": "Hong Kong luxury retail market growth 2024 2025 premiumisation trends drivers inbound tourists"}, "output": {"id": null, "name": "market_research", "type": "tool", "status": "success", "content": "## Market Research: Hong Kong luxury retail market growth 2024 2025 premiumisation trends drivers inbound tourists\\n\\n### Top Search Results\\n\\n1. **Mainland China and Hong Kong Luxury Market**\\n   Notes: 1) PwC China forecast for market size covers 6 categories incl. 'Apparel and Footwear, Leather Goods, Premium Beauty and Personal Care, Jewellery and ...Read more\\n   Source: https://www.pwccn.com/en/retail-and-consumer/mainland-china-hong-kong-luxury-market-apr2024.pdf\\n\\n2. **Hong Kong Luxury Sales Maintain Upward Trend in March**\\n   6 May 2026 — The government expects retail sales to continue their positive trajectory as the local market recovers, thanks to growth from inbound tourism ...Read more\\n   Source: https://rapaport.com/news/hong-kong-luxury-sales-maintain-upward-trend-in-march/\\n\\n3. **Hong Kong Tourism Market Outlook 2025 to 2035**\\n   22 Apr 2025 — Spending by visitors to Hong Kong Tourism Market is projected to reach USD 7.1 billion in 2025, powered by much-revived cross-border travel.Read more\\n   Source: https://www.futuremarketinsights.com/reports/hong-kong-tourism-spend-analysis-forecast\\n\\n4. **Hong Kong Luxury Goods Retailing Market Trends 2026**\\n   Hong Kong Luxury Goods Retailing Market size was valued at USD XX Billion in 2024 and is projected to reach USD XX Billion by 2033, ...\\n   Source: https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/hong-kong-luxury-goods-retailing-market-trends-tbf3f/\\n\\n5. **China Luxury Consumer Forecast 2025 Report - MDRi**\\n   The strong consumer demand for luxury watches, handbags, jewellery, and travel experiences positions these categories as key growth drivers for the industry.Read more\\n   Source: https://mdr-i.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/china-luxury-consumer-forecast-2025-report-9336d62f70f05b1786a0ba9471f59c86.pdf\\n\\n### Related topics: Bain luxury report 2025 pdf, BCG luxury report 2025, Deloitte Global Powers of luxury goods 2025, Luxury goods Worldwide market Study, Global 2025 premium luxury performance high-end brands\\n", "artifact": null, "tool_call_id": "call_Y8AHVxQlVOQvztGcKwF99ZdK", "additional_kwargs": {}, "response_metadata": {}}}, "name": "market_research", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"todos": [{"status": "completed", "content": "Run market_research for Hong Kong retail market size, growth, luxury/premium segment trends, key drivers"}, {"status": "completed", "content": "Run market_research for Causeway Bay retail/foot-traffic trends and flagship store importance; competitor density themes"}, {"status": "completed", "content": "Run market_research for HK regulatory context for retail fit-out (building permits, fire safety, licensing), labour, consumer, and digital privacy considerations"}, {"status": "completed", "content": "Run market_research for ESG/sustainability considerations for retail fit-outs in Hong Kong (energy efficiency, waste, green building)"}]}}, "name": "write_todos", "event": "on_tool_start"}, {"data": {"input": {"todos": [{"status": "completed", "content": "Run market_research for Hong Kong retail market size, growth, luxury/premium segment trends, key drivers"}, {"status": "completed", "content": "Run market_research for Causeway Bay retail/foot-traffic trends and flagship store importance; competitor density themes"}, {"status": "completed", "content": "Run market_research for HK regulatory context for retail fit-out (building permits, fire safety, licensing), labour, consumer, and digital privacy considerations"}, {"status": "completed", "content": "Run market_research for ESG/sustainability considerations for retail fit-outs in Hong Kong (energy efficiency, waste, green building)"}]}, "output": "Command(update={'todos': [{'content': 'Run market_research for Hong Kong retail market size, growth, luxury/premium segment trends, key drivers', 'status': 'completed'}, {'content': 'Run market_research for Causeway Bay retail/foot-traffic trends and flagship store importance; competitor density themes', 'status': 'completed'}, {'content': 'Run market_research for HK regulatory context for retail fit-out (building permits, fire safety, licensing), labour, consumer, and digital privacy considerations', 'status': 'completed'}, {'content': 'Run market_research for ESG/sustainability considerations for retail fit-outs in Hong Kong (energy efficiency, waste, green building)', 'status': 'completed'}], 'messages': [ToolMessage(content=\\"Updated todo list to [{'content': 'Run market_research for Hong Kong retail market size, growth, luxury/premium segment trends, key drivers', 'status': 'completed'}, {'content': 'Run market_research for Causeway Bay retail/foot-traffic trends and flagship store importance; competitor density themes', 'status': 'completed'}, {'content': 'Run market_research for HK regulatory context for retail fit-out (building permits, fire safety, licensing), labour, consumer, and digital privacy considerations', 'status': 'completed'}, {'content': 'Run market_research for ESG/sustainability considerations for retail fit-outs in Hong Kong (energy efficiency, waste, green building)', 'status': 'completed'}]\\", tool_call_id='call_f95bXwphwnKsvljkERM0MuWc')]})"}, "name": "write_todos", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"description": "Research market size, growth, competitors, and regulatory context for the following full project JSON. Return a structured research output that can be embedded into the business case. PROJECT JSON:\\n{\\n  \\"project_name\\": \\"Causeway Bay Flagship Store Expansion\\",\\n  \\"project_type\\": \\"CAPEX\\",\\n  \\"sponsor\\": \\"Alice Wong, Chief Commercial Officer\\",\\n  \\"project_manager\\": \\"Ben Lam, Senior Project Manager\\",\\n  \\"business_unit\\": \\"Retail Operations\\",\\n  \\"capex_hkd_millions\\": 5.0,\\n  \\"description\\": \\"Expand the existing Causeway Bay store from 3,000 sq ft to 6,000 sq ft by taking over the adjacent unit. The expanded space will house a new premium product line and in-store experience zone to drive higher average basket size and foot traffic.\\",\\n  \\"assumptions\\": {\\n    \\"lease_term_years\\": 5,\\n    \\"fit_out_cost_hkd_millions\\": 3.0,\\n    \\"equipment_cost_hkd_millions\\": 1.5,\\n    \\"contingency_hkd_millions\\": 0.5,\\n    \\"revenue_year1_hkd_millions\\": 8.0,\\n    \\"revenue_growth_pct_pa\\": 10,\\n    \\"gross_margin_pct\\": 42,\\n    \\"occupancy_cost_pct_of_revenue\\": 15,\\n    \\"staff_cost_hkd_millions_pa\\": 1.2,\\n    \\"opening_date\\": \\"Q3 2026\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"attachments\\": [],\\n  \\"known_market_data\\": {\\n    \\"hong_kong_retail_sales_growth_2025_pct\\": 4.5,\\n    \\"luxury_retail_segment_growth_pct\\": 6.2,\\n    \\"causeway_bay_foot_traffic_index\\": 98\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nRESEARCH REQUIREMENTS:\\n- Market overview for Hong Kong retail with emphasis on premium/luxury segments; cite indicative figures and growth drivers.\\n- Causeway Bay retail context: foot traffic trends, relevance of flagship stores, nearby competitor density (no need for exhaustive list; provide examples and themes).\\n- Competitive landscape: types of retailers that compete for premium product lines and experience-based retail; summarize positioning, typical tactics, and differentiation.\\n- Customer insights: shopping behavior trends in HK (e.g., experiential retail, premiumisation) and implications for basket size/footfall.\\n- Regulatory/legal context relevant to HK retail CAPEX/fit-out: e.g., building/works approvals, fire safety and licensing considerations, consumer protection basics, labour considerations, data privacy if experience zone uses digital elements (high-level).\\n- Any relevant ESG/sustainability considerations for retail fit-outs in HK (e.g., waste management, energy efficiency) at high level.\\n- Provide a short “Implications for this project” section mapping research findings to the business case assumptions (revenue growth, margin, costs, lease term).\\n\\nOUTPUT FORMAT (must be machine-includable into later tasks):\\n- Executive research summary (bullets)\\n- Market & segment context (HK retail, luxury/premium)\\n- Location & demand drivers (Causeway Bay)\\n- Competitive landscape (themes + examples)\\n- Customer & shopping behavior insights\\n- Regulatory & compliance context (fit-out/occupancy/safety; labour; consumer; digital privacy if any)\\n- ESG considerations (fit-out)\\n- Implications for this project (explicit bullet mapping to the assumptions)\\n- Sources list (bullet list of key references; if exact URLs unavailable, provide credible source names and what they likely contain).", "subagent_type": "research-agent"}, "output": "Command(update={'files': {}, 'messages': [ToolMessage(content='## Executive research summary (for business case embedding)\\\\n- **HK retail market (macro):** Retail sales value growth has been **modest/uneven** in recent periods, with year-on-year changes varying by month; **tourism recovery/inbound visitors** is a key demand stabiliser and growth driver.\\\\n- **Premium/luxury segment momentum:** Luxury/premium categories in HK have shown **upward trend signals** linked to **inbound tourism, high-end brand assortment, and “premiumisation”** (consumers trading up to better experiences/products).\\\\n- **Causeway Bay demand profile:** Causeway Bay is a **high-footfall, prime retail cluster** (multiple connected malls + dense street retail) that remains attractive for **flagship and premium placements**; leasing momentum/retail activity has been reported as **concentrated in Causeway Bay** in recent market updates.\\\\n- **Competitive landscape:** Premium product lines compete on **store format + experience + omnichannel** (e.g., appointment/concierge service, interactive zones, seasonal activations, exclusive drops, brand storytelling).\\\\n- **Customer shopping behavior:** HK shoppers (locals + tourists) increasingly respond to **experiential, curated, and digitally enabled** in-store journeys—supporting the business case rationale for an **experience zone** to lift **basket size and revisit intent**.\\\\n- **Regulatory/compliance focus for fit-out/operations:** Key risks concentrate on **building/works approvals**, **fire safety compliance and certification**, **licensing requirements tied to premises type**, **employment law (wages/working conditions)**, **consumer protection (trade descriptions/refunds/accurate info)**, and **personal data protection** if the experience zone uses any customer data capture (CCTV, Wi‑Fi tracking, apps).\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Market & segment context (HK retail; premium/luxury emphasis)\\\\n- **Overall retail backdrop:** Recent official and industry commentary indicates **retail sales value growth has been low-to-moderate**, with volatility by month. This typically increases the importance of **conversion levers** (store experience, traffic generation, and merchandising) rather than relying solely on broad market growth.\\\\n- **Premiumisation & luxury performance drivers:**\\\\n  - **Inbound tourism** (spend and store visits) is a primary support for HK’s luxury/premium categories.\\\\n  - **Category premiumisation**: consumers gravitate toward better quality, limited editions, and “premium experiences” rather than purely price-based shopping.\\\\n  - **Store format as a differentiator:** brands invest in **flagship formats**, curated floors, and experiential zones to justify premium pricing and improve conversion.\\\\n\\\\n**Indicative research references (not project financial calculations):**\\\\n- PwC “Mainland China and Hong Kong Luxury Market” (2024) — includes luxury market size/forecast framing and category coverage. *(Source from search results below.)*\\\\n- Industry/press references linking luxury demand to tourism recovery. *(Source from search results below.)*\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Location & demand drivers (Causeway Bay)\\\\n- **Prime, pedestrian-dense retail ecosystem:** Causeway Bay is characterised as a **major shopping district** with **multiple prime malls** and extensive retail streets—supporting sustained footfall for premium formats.\\\\n- **Flagship store relevance:**\\\\n  - Prime malls and precincts in Causeway Bay are repeatedly positioned as **best-in-class locations for “ultra-luxe” brand presence** (brand visibility + customer spillover from neighboring anchors).\\\\n  - Recent real-estate/market updates highlight **active leasing activity** in districts including **Causeway Bay**, supported by **tourist footfall** (marketbeat-style reporting).\\\\n- **Foot traffic implications for expansion:** Expanding into an adjacent unit typically aims to:\\\\n  - improve **shopper dwell time** (more “reasons to stay” via experience zone),\\\\n  - strengthen **merchandising breadth** (premium line + hero displays),\\\\n  - reduce **friction** (better flow and product discovery).\\\\n\\\\n**Indicative research references:**\\\\n- InvestHK / market positioning material on Causeway Bay as part of a “prime shopping” ecosystem (“Twenty-minute city” style retail access narrative).\\\\n- Cushman & Wakefield Hong Kong retail market updates referencing **Causeway Bay leasing/tourist footfall**.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Competitive landscape (themes + examples)\\\\n**Core competitive themes for premium/experience-based retail in HK**\\\\n1. **Flagship-as-media:** Large-format stores used for brand storytelling, product theatre, and repeatable “moments” (launch events, seasonal installations).\\\\n2. **Service-led premiumisation:** Appointment/concierge flows, staff-led product discovery, and curated service experiences that justify higher price points.\\\\n3. **Experiential zones + interactive retail:** Try-on, demonstration, personalization, limited-edition “drops,” and immersive displays.\\\\n4. **Omnichannel integration:** Click-and-collect, in-store digital assistance, loyalty apps, and seamless service between online and physical store.\\\\n5. **Cross-tenant/precinct synergy:** Competitors benefit from dense foot traffic and brand clustering in malls/precincts, so differentiation must be **within** the store experience, not only location.\\\\n\\\\n**Examples (illustrative, from search results)**\\\\n- Causeway Bay luxury/flagship destinations include **major luxury boutiques at landmark/major mall precincts** (e.g., Lee Gardens precinct and other prime malls mentioned in guides).\\\\n- Experience-led retail is aligned with broader Hong Kong retail trend commentary around **immersive/interactive store experiences**.\\\\n\\\\n*(Note: the research returned “examples and themes” rather than a comprehensive competitor list; this matches your requirement.)*\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Customer & shopping behavior insights (implications for basket size & footfall)\\\\n- **Experiential retail is a conversion lever:** Customers increasingly evaluate physical shopping by “what else” the store offers (interaction, guided discovery, events), not only product availability.\\\\n- **Premiumisation behavior:** Higher-income locals and tourists show stronger willingness to trade up when:\\\\n  - the premium line is clearly curated and visible,\\\\n  - the store offers “confidence” signals (expert staff, brand heritage, service quality),\\\\n  - the experience feels worth the price differential.\\\\n- **Traffic-to-spend conversion:** Experience zones can:\\\\n  - increase dwell time (more exposure to premium assortment),\\\\n  - support add-on purchases (complementary items promoted in the experience flow),\\\\n  - encourage repeat visitation via events and newness.\\\\n\\\\n**Indicative research reference**\\\\n- Cushman & Wakefield “Hong Kong Experiential Retail Report 2023” (from search results) — focuses on evolving preferences and both tourists/locals.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Regulatory & compliance context (HK retail CAPEX/fit-out; occupancy; safety; labour; consumer; digital privacy)\\\\n### 1) Fit-out / building works approvals & process\\\\n- **Building works and approvals:** Retail fit-outs typically require **formal approval/consent** processes with the **Buildings Department** depending on scope, and may be subject to **minor works control** or full approvals depending on classification.\\\\n- **Fire safety approvals before commissioning/works that affect fire services:** The **Fire Services Department (FSD)** process is critical—works that affect fire services generally require **prior approval** before commencement.\\\\n\\\\n### 2) Fire safety requirements (high-risk area)\\\\n- **Fire safety ordinance / licensing regimes:** HK has specific fire safety legislation covering commercial premises and buildings; compliance is expected for design (means of escape, fire services installations, detection/suppression where applicable) and certification/inspection.\\\\n- Practical implications for a store expansion:\\\\n  - layout changes must respect **means of escape** and **travel distances**,\\\\n  - any modification affecting fire installations requires coordinated approvals and testing/certification.\\\\n\\\\n**Key sources from search results**\\\\n- Cap. 502 “Fire Safety (Commercial Premises) Ordinance”\\\\n- Cap. 572 “Fire Safety (Buildings) Ordinance”\\\\n- FSD materials on licensing/certification and guidance/code documents (means of escape, minimum fire service installations).\\\\n\\\\n### 3) Labour considerations (employment ordinance basics)\\\\n- **Minimum wage (statutory):** HK statutory minimum wage applies across workers and must be budgeted for.\\\\n- **Employment Ordinance guidance:** The **Employment Ordinance** framework (working hours rules for specified groups, rest days/holiday entitlements, record-keeping expectations) drives compliance for staffing plans and any event staffing.\\\\n\\\\n### 4) Consumer protection (retail sales conduct)\\\\n- **Trade descriptions / accurate representations:** HK includes consumer protection mechanisms under laws such as **Trade Descriptions Ordinance** and the broader consumer rights framework.\\\\n- **Sale of goods/service contract protections:** “Supply of goods as agreed” principles affect returns/refunds handling and customer communications.\\\\n- For an experience zone: ensure any promotional claims (pricing, exclusivity, limited offers, authenticity, services) are **substantiated and clearly disclosed**.\\\\n\\\\n### 5) Digital privacy (if the experience zone uses digital elements)\\\\n- **Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance (PDPO, Cap. 486):** governs collection/use of personal data.\\\\n- **CCTV / surveillance guidance:** if the experience zone uses CCTV or similar tracking, align with PDPO principles and F/PCPD guidance on responsible CCTV use (notice, purpose limitation, retention, security).\\\\n- **If using Wi‑Fi/app/member data:** ensure consent/notice and lawful purpose, and apply data minimisation/security controls.\\\\n\\\\n**Key sources from search results**\\\\n- PCPD guidance on CCTV surveillance\\\\n- PDPO overviews\\\\n\\\\n**Regulatory risk flag (for business case governance)**\\\\n- **Primary CAPEX risk:** schedule slippage if fire services approvals/certification steps are not planned early.\\\\n- **Primary operating risk:** data privacy non-compliance if any customer-identifying capture is used without proper notices/controls.\\\\n- **Primary HR risk:** wage/working-hours compliance for additional staffing during launch and ongoing operations.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## ESG considerations (fit-out sustainability in HK; high-level)\\\\n- **Green building frameworks:** Hong Kong commonly uses **BEAM Plus** (HK Green Building Council) as a voluntary/market-recognised assessment scheme for sustainability performance.\\\\n- **Fit-out ESG areas to consider:**\\\\n  - **Energy efficiency** (HVAC/lighting controls, refrigeration efficiency for product areas if relevant),\\\\n  - **materials management** (low-VOC, responsible sourcing),\\\\n  - **waste management** (construction waste reduction, recycling plans),\\\\n  - **commissioning/ongoing building performance** alignment.\\\\n\\\\n**Key sources from search results**\\\\n- BEAM Plus New Buildings v2.0 and related documentation.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Implications for this project (explicit mapping to the business case assumptions)\\\\n- **Revenue growth (assumption: 10% CAGR / PA):**\\\\n  - Supported by macro: premium demand stability tends to track **tourism/inbound recovery** and the “premiumisation” trend.\\\\n  - Supported by micro: expanding into an adjacent unit enables **larger premium assortment + more experience content**, improving conversion from footfall into sales (experience-led retail trend).\\\\n- **Revenue Year 1 (assumption: HKD 8.0m):**\\\\n  - Feasible rationale linked to Causeway Bay’s **prime footfall ecosystem** and premium retailer clustering/anchor synergy (store expansion increases capacity to capture demand).\\\\n- **Gross margin (assumption: 42%):**\\\\n  - Experience/flagship differentiation typically supports **premium pricing power** and higher mix of premium product line (qualitative support from premiumisation theme).\\\\n  - Ensure margin does not get eroded by experience costs that scale disproportionately.\\\\n- **Occupancy cost % of revenue (assumption: 15%):**\\\\n  - Fit-out/adjacent unit expansion should be assessed against leasing economics and potential rent step-up; the competitive leasing activity in Causeway Bay suggests the market values prime space (but actual rent inputs must be validated).\\\\n- **Staff cost (assumption: HKD 1.2m PA):**\\\\n  - Labour compliance requirements (minimum wage + Employment Ordinance operational rules) imply staffing budgets should incorporate not only headcount but compliance-driven scheduling and event staffing overhead.\\\\n- **Lease term (assumption: 5 years):**\\\\n  - Regulatory processes (fire safety approvals + fit-out certification) should be planned to avoid loss of revenue time near opening.\\\\n  - Digital privacy governance (PDPO) should be operationalized at launch to avoid remediation costs mid-lease.\\\\n- **Opening timing (assumption: Q3 2026):**\\\\n  - Fire safety and building approvals are critical-path; schedule buffers should reflect the risk of approvals/certifications.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Sources list (key references from the research)\\\\n- **CENSTATD (Hong Kong Census and Statistics Department)** – retail sales statistics and provisional monthly retail sales releases (year-on-year growth context).\\\\n- **PwC (2024) – “Mainland China and Hong Kong Luxury Market”** – luxury market outlook/forecast framing by categories (premiumisation context).\\\\n- **Cushman & Wakefield – Hong Kong Retail MarketBeat Q3 2025** – district-level retail leasing activity and demand drivers (includes Causeway Bay/tourist footfall references).\\\\n- **InvestHK – “Consumer Products: Retailing in the Twenty-Minute City” (2022)** – Causeway Bay/major retail district positioning and accessibility narrative.\\\\n- **Hong Kong Fire Services Department (FSD)** – premises/fire safety licensing and requirements documentation; approval expectations for works affecting fire safety.\\\\n- **Hong Kong Legislation (elegislation.gov.hk)** – **Cap. 502 Fire Safety (Commercial Premises) Ordinance**; **Cap. 572 Fire Safety (Buildings) Ordinance**.\\\\n- **Labour Department / Employment Ordinance guidance** – employment compliance framework; minimum wage information.\\\\n- **Consumer Council / CLIC / relevant HK consumer protection sources** – consumer rights and complaint context; consumer protection principles (trade descriptions/sale of goods basics).\\\\n- **Privacy Commissioner for Personal Data (PCPD)** – guidance on responsible **CCTV surveillance** use; PDPO compliance principles.\\\\n- **HK Green Building Council – BEAM Plus documentation** – sustainability assessment framework for buildings/projects.\\\\n\\\\nIf you share the project’s **industry/category** (e.g., cosmetics, fashion, electronics, food & beverage) and whether the experience zone uses **CCTV, Wi‑Fi, a loyalty app, or QR check-ins**, I can tighten the competitor and regulatory sections to be more specific to likely store practices.', tool_call_id='call_y2IfAaLR7AYHm4zzyQKdKSNZ')]})"}, "name": "task", "event": "on_tool_end"}, {"data": {"input": {"description": "Compute IRR, NPV@20% (pre-tax), payback period, CAGR, sensitivity table, and KPI set for the following full project JSON.\\n\\nPROJECT JSON:\\n{\\n  \\"project_name\\": \\"Causeway Bay Flagship Store Expansion\\",\\n  \\"project_type\\": \\"CAPEX\\",\\n  \\"sponsor\\": \\"Alice Wong, Chief Commercial Officer\\",\\n  \\"project_manager\\": \\"Ben Lam, Senior Project Manager\\",\\n  \\"business_unit\\": \\"Retail Operations\\",\\n  \\"capex_hkd_millions\\": 5.0,\\n  \\"description\\": \\"Expand the existing Causeway Bay store from 3,000 sq ft to 6,000 sq ft by taking over the adjacent unit. The expanded space will house a new premium product line and in-store experience zone to drive higher average basket size and foot traffic.\\",\\n  \\"assumptions\\": {\\n    \\"lease_term_years\\": 5,\\n    \\"fit_out_cost_hkd_millions\\": 3.0,\\n    \\"equipment_cost_hkd_millions\\": 1.5,\\n    \\"contingency_hkd_millions\\": 0.5,\\n    \\"revenue_year1_hkd_millions\\": 8.0,\\n    \\"revenue_growth_pct_pa\\": 10,\\n    \\"gross_margin_pct\\": 42,\\n    \\"occupancy_cost_pct_of_revenue\\": 15,\\n    \\"staff_cost_hkd_millions_pa\\": 1.2,\\n    \\"opening_date\\": \\"Q3 2026\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"attachments\\": [],\\n  \\"known_market_data\\": {\\n    \\"hong_kong_retail_sales_growth_2025_pct\\": 4.5,\\n    \\"luxury_retail_segment_growth_pct\\": 6.2,\\n    \\"causeway_bay_foot_traffic_index\\": 98\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nRESEARCH CONTEXT (from prior step):\\n- HK retail market macro: modest/uneven retail sales growth; inbound tourism as key stabiliser.\\n- Premium/luxury: upward trend signals linked to inbound tourism and premiumisation.\\n- Causeway Bay: prime, high-footfall cluster with strong relevance for flagship/premium placements.\\n- Customer: experiential retail trend supports higher conversion, basket size, dwell time.\\n- Competitive: premium/experience-led store formats, omnichannel, service-led premiumisation.\\n- Regulatory/compliance: fit-out approvals, fire safety licensing/certification critical-path; Employment Ordinance and minimum wage; consumer protection; PDPO if digital/experience zone uses CCTV/Wi‑Fi/app.\\n- ESG: consider BEAM Plus and energy efficiency, waste management, low-VOC materials.\\n- Implications for assumptions: rationale for 10% revenue growth via expanded premium assortment + experience; margin supported by premium line; occupancy/staff budgets must be validated and compliance planned; opening Q3 2026 requires fire safety approval planning.\\n\\nREQUIREMENTS:\\n- Use discount rate 20% pre-tax and assessment period default 5 years.\\n- Model cashflows based on provided assumptions. If timing is needed for CAPEX vs opening, assume CAPEX occurs at/around opening year start unless otherwise implied; state clearly any timing convention you adopt.\\n- Compute: IRR, NPV@20%, payback period (in years), CAGR of revenue (and/or profit if you choose—state which), and a sensitivity table (at minimum vary revenue_growth and gross_margin or revenue_year1; include assumptions used).\\n- Determine KPI set according to rule: 3 if CAPEX > HK$10M | 1 if > HK$2M | 0 optional if ≤ HK$2M. Here CAPEX is HK$5.0M so KPIs count = 1.\\n- Apply failure threshold logic: 50% otherwise (since CAPEX < HK$20M). Use this to comment on whether project passes.\\n- Red flag checks: flag if computed IRR > 100% or gross margin > 50%.\\n- Return results in a structured format suitable for embedding into writer-agent.\\n\\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\\n- Financial summary (capex, discount rate, period, timing assumptions)\\n- Year-by-year key metrics table (revenue, gross profit, occupancy cost, staff cost, implied operating cashflow or EBITDA proxy, free cashflow) for 5 years\\n- IRR, NPV@20%, payback, CAGR\\n- Sensitivity table with scenarios and resulting NPV and/or IRR\\n- KPI set (exact KPI name, definition, target, baseline, measurement cadence)\\n- Pass/fail against failure threshold and red-flag notes\\n", "subagent_type": "finance-agent"}}, "name": "task", "event": "on_tool_start"}, {"data": {"input": {"todos": [{"status": "in_progress", "content": "Derive annual cashflows (year 0 to year 5) from provided assumptions, including timing convention for CAPEX vs opening."}, {"status": "pending", "content": "Compute financial metrics (IRR, NPV@20%, payback, CAGR) using financial_calculator with discount_rate=20%."}, {"status": "pending", "content": "Generate sensitivity scenarios using sensitivi